gine/godot/pull/123660.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Closes #123651\r\n\r\nEditing a project's tags in the Project Manager loads and saves\r\n`project.godot` through a throwaway `ProjectSettings` instance, even\r\nthough only `application/config/tags` is touched.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n`_apply_project_tags()` now loads and saves `project.godot` with\r\n`ConfigFile` instead of constructing and destroying a full\r\n`ProjectSettings` object. The load-failure message now includes the\r\nactual `Error` code rather than assuming the file is missing/corrupted.\r\n\r\n### Testing\r\n\r\n- Opened the Project Manager, added tag to a project from godot 4.6 and it didn't change project version.\r\n- Renamed `project.godot` away and confirmed the error dialog reports the error code and the tags dialog is re-shown.\r\n\r\n### AI disclosure\r\n\r\nThe change was authored by me. AI assistance was limited to code\r\ncompletion and review of the C++ edit. I understand and take\r\nresponsibility for the submitted code.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123660/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123660/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}